# Copy to apps/web/.env (gitignored) to point the app at a deployed Fleet API.
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_ to the browser bundle, and only at
# build time — `pnpm dev` and `pnpm build` read this file, nothing reads it at
# runtime. src/data/fleet-source-selection.ts is where the value is validated.
#
# Empty or absent — the default for local dev and for every test — runs the
# in-memory demo fleet: deterministic sites, no network, no API needed. Set it
# to the API's origin (scheme and host, no trailing path) for live mode, e.g.
# https://abc123.execute-api.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com. A value that is not an
# http(s) URL fails the app loudly at startup rather than falling back.
#
# Reads work as soon as this is set. Browser *writes* (adding a site) need the
# API to allow this origin too: the dev server's http://localhost:5173 must be
# in the API stack's `web_origins` — see infra/api/api.auto.tfvars.example.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
